:name: R4 - stand in for the machine state the ESP32-S2 boot ROM would have left
:description:
:description: The esp32s2-sesame platform has NO boot ROM (see the .repl, note 3), so
:description: nothing establishes the processor state an ESP32-S2 application entry
:description: point is entitled to assume. Measured reset state on Renode 1.16.1
:description: immediately after LoadELF (emulator/renode/tests/logs/r4-resetstate.log):
:description:
:description:     PS 0x0000001F  (WOE=0, EXCM=1, INTLEVEL=15)   VECBASE 0x40000000
:description:     WINDOWBASE 0   WINDOWSTART 0                   a1 (SP) 0x00000000
:description:
:description: That is the architectural Xtensa reset state and Renode is right to
:description: produce it; on silicon the mask ROM sets PS/SP up long before the app
:description: entry point runs.
:description:
:description: `call_start_cpu0` begins with `entry a1, 48`, and tlib's helper_entry
:description: raises IllegalInstruction unless (PS & (WOE|EXCM)) == WOE, so the very
:description: first instruction of every Arduino/ESP-IDF image faults without this.
:description:
:description: PS is settable from the monitor. The address registers are NOT: on
:description: Renode 1.16.1 `cpu SetRegister <n>` / `SetRegister "AR1"` silently
:description: no-op for the Xtensa AR file and `GetRegister` always reads 0x0
:description: (emulator/renode/tests/logs/r4-setreg.log). So the stack pointer is
:description: installed by a three-instruction trampoline written into unused IRAM
:description: at the top of the iram window, which the caller jumps to instead of
:description: the ELF entry point:
:description:
:description:     0x4006FEF8: .word 0x3FFFE70C     SOC_ROM_STACK_START
:description:     0x4006FEFC: .word <entry>        patched by the caller
:description:     0x4006FF00: l32r a1, -8          load SP
:description:     0x4006FF03: l32r a8, -8          load entry
:description:     0x4006FF06: jx   a8
:description:
:description: Encodings verified with `cpu DisassembleBlock`
:description: (emulator/renode/tests/logs/r4-asm.log).
:description:
:description: Values:
:description:   PS 0x00050020 = WOE(0x40000) | CALLINC=1(0x10000) | UM(0x20),
:description:                   EXCM=0, INTLEVEL=0 - the value R2 section 3.4 read back
:description:                   from a live windowed frame on this same core.
:description:   WINDOWSTART 0x1 - one live frame at WINDOWBASE 0.
:description:   SP 0x3FFFE70C = SOC_ROM_STACK_START, from esp32s2-libs/3.3.11/
:description:                   include/soc/esp32s2/include/soc/soc.h:207 - literally
:description:                   the stack pointer the ROM hands over.
:description:
:description: Caller contract: set $entry to the ELF entry point before including.
:description: This is a HARNESS-SIDE stand-in for a boot ROM, not a model of one.

cpu PS 0x00050020
cpu WINDOWBASE 0x0
cpu WINDOWSTART 0x1

sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x4006FEF8 0x3FFFE70C
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x4006FEFC $entry
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x4006FF00 0x81FFFE11
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x4006FF04 0x08A0FFFE
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x4006FF08 0x00000000

cpu PC 0x4006FF00

echo "### bootstate applied - PS / WINDOWSTART / SP trampoline at 0x4006FF00"
cpu PS
cpu DisassembleBlock 0x4006FF00 9
